\p \v 1 \w Soon|strong="H1961"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w began to complain|strong="H596"\w* \w about their hardship|strong="H7451"\w* \w in the hearing|strong="H241"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w and when He|strong="H3068"\w* \w heard them|strong="H8085"\w*, \w His anger|strong="H639"\w* \w was kindled|strong="H2734"\w*, \w and fire|strong="H784"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w blazed|strong="H1197"\w* among them \w and consumed|strong="H398"\w* \w the outskirts|strong="H7097"\w* \w of the camp|strong="H4264"\w*. \v 2 \w And the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w cried out|strong="H6817"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \w and he|strong="H4872"\w* \w prayed|strong="H6419"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w and the fire|strong="H784"\w* \w died down|strong="H8257"\w*. \v 3 \w So that|strong="H1931"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w was called|strong="H7121"\w* \w Taberah|strong="H8404"\w*,\f + \fr 11:3 \fqa Taberah \ft means \fqa burning\ft .\f* \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w the fire|strong="H784"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had burned|strong="H1197"\w* among them.
