\s1 The Quail and the Plague
\p \v 31 \w Now a wind|strong="H7307"\w* \w sent by|strong="H4480"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came up|strong="H5265"\w*, \w drove in|strong="H1468"\w* \w quail|strong="H7958"\w* \w from|strong="H854"\w* \w the sea|strong="H3220"\w*, \w and brought them|strong="H5203"\w* \w near|strong="H5921"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w*, \w about two cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w above|strong="H5921"\w* \w the surface|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the ground|strong="H776"\w*,\f + \fr 11:31 \ft Or \fqa up to two cubits deep\ft ; that is, \ref approximately 3|3\ref* feet or 91.4 centimeters\f* \w for a day’s|strong="H3117"\w* \w journey|strong="H1870"\w* \w in every direction|strong="H3541"\w* \w around|strong="H5439"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w*. \v 32 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w and night|strong="H3915"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the next|strong="H4283"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*, \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w stayed up|strong="H6965"\w* \w gathering|strong="H622"\w* \w the quail|strong="H7958"\w*. \w No one gathered|strong="H622"\w* \w less than|strong="H4591"\w* \w ten|strong="H6235"\w* \w homers|strong="H2563"\w*,\f + \fr 11:32 \fqa \ref 10|0\ref* homers\ft is \ref approximately 62|62\ref*.4 bushels or 2,200 liters.\f* \w and they spread them out|strong="H7849"\w* \w all around|strong="H5439"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w*.
