\c 12
\s1 The Complaint of Miriam and Aaron
\p \v 1 \w Then Miriam|strong="H4813"\w* \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w criticized|strong="H1696"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w because of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Cushite|strong="H3569"\w* \w woman|strong="H802"\w* \w he had married|strong="H3947"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w he had taken|strong="H3947"\w* \w a Cushite|strong="H3569"\w* \w wife|strong="H802"\w*. \v 2 “\w Does the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w only|strong="H7535"\w* \w through Moses|strong="H4872"\w*?” \w they said|strong="H559"\w*. “\w Does He not|strong="H3808"\w* \w also|strong="H1571"\w* \w speak|strong="H1696"\w* through us?” \w And the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w heard this|strong="H8085"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w Now Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w was a very|strong="H3966"\w* \w humble|strong="H6035"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w*, \w more so than any|strong="H3605"\w* \w man|strong="H120"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the face|strong="H6440"\w* \w of the earth|strong="H127"\w*.
\p \v 4 \w And suddenly|strong="H6597"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w*, \w and Miriam|strong="H4813"\w*, “\w You three|strong="H7969"\w*, \w come out|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w* \w of Meeting|strong="H4150"\w*.” \w So the three|strong="H7969"\w* \w went out|strong="H3318"\w*, \v 5 \w and the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came down|strong="H3381"\w* \w in a pillar|strong="H5982"\w* \w of cloud|strong="H6051"\w*, \w stood|strong="H5975"\w* \w at the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w to the Tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w and summoned|strong="H7121"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and Miriam|strong="H4813"\w*. \w When both|strong="H8147"\w* \w of them had stepped forward|strong="H3318"\w*, \v 6 \w He said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w Hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w now|strong="H4994"\w* \w My words|strong="H1697"\w*:
\q1 \w If|strong="H518"\w* \w there is|strong="H1961"\w* \w a prophet among you|strong="H5030"\w*,
\q2 \w I, the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w will reveal Myself|strong="H3045"\w* \w to him|strong="H413"\w* \w in a vision|strong="H4759"\w*;
\q2 \w I will speak|strong="H1696"\w* to him \w in a dream|strong="H2472"\w*.
\q1 \v 7 \w But this is not|strong="H3808"\w* \w so|strong="H3651"\w* \w with My servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*;
\q2 \w he|strong="H1931"\w* \w is faithful|strong="H539"\w* \w in all|strong="H3605"\w* \w My house|strong="H1004"\w*.\f + \fr 12:7 \ft Cited in \ref Hebrews 3:5|HEB 3:5\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 8 \w I speak|strong="H1696"\w* with him \w face|strong="H6310"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w face|strong="H6310"\w*,
\q2 \w clearly|strong="H4758"\w* \w and not|strong="H3808"\w* \w in riddles|strong="H2420"\w*;
\q2 \w he sees|strong="H5027"\w* \w the form|strong="H8544"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
\p \w Why then|strong="H4069"\w* \w were you unafraid|strong="H3372"\w* \w to speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w against My servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*?” \v 9 \w So the anger|strong="H639"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w burned|strong="H2734"\w* against them, \w and He departed|strong="H1980"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w As the cloud|strong="H6051"\w* \w lifted|strong="H5493"\w* \w from above|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Tent|strong="H168"\w*, \w suddenly|strong="H2009"\w* \w Miriam|strong="H4813"\w* \w became leprous|strong="H6879"\w*,\f + \fr 12:10 \ft The Hebrew word traditionally translated as \fqa leprous\ft was used for various skin diseases; see \ref Leviticus 13|LEV 13\ref*.\f* \w white as snow|strong="H7950"\w*. \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w turned|strong="H6437"\w* \w toward|strong="H413"\w* \w her|strong="H4813"\w*, \w saw that|strong="H2009"\w* \w she was leprous|strong="H6879"\w*, \v 11 \w and said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, “\w My lord|strong="H113"\w*, \w please|strong="H4994"\w* \w do not|strong="H408"\w* \w hold|strong="H7896"\w* \w against us|strong="H5921"\w* \w this sin|strong="H2403"\w* \w we have so foolishly|strong="H2973"\w* \w committed|strong="H2398"\w*. \v 12 \w Please|strong="H4994"\w* \w do not|strong="H408"\w* \w let her be|strong="H1961"\w* \w like a stillborn infant|strong="H4191"\w* \w whose|strong="H834"\w* \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w is half|strong="H2677"\w* \w consumed|strong="H398"\w* \w when he comes out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of his mother’s|strong="H517"\w* \w womb|strong="H7358"\w*.”
\p \v 13 \w So Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w cried out|strong="H6817"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, “\w O God|strong="H410"\w*, \w please|strong="H4994"\w* \w heal|strong="H7495"\w* her!”
\p \v 14 \w But the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w answered|strong="H559"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, “\w If her father|strong="H1"\w* \w had but spit|strong="H3417"\w* \w in her face|strong="H6440"\w*, \w would she not|strong="H3808"\w* \w have been in disgrace|strong="H3637"\w* \w for seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w*? \w Let her be confined|strong="H5462"\w* \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w for seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w*; \w after that|strong="H310"\w* \w she may be brought back in|strong="H622"\w*.”
\p \v 15 \w So Miriam|strong="H4813"\w* \w was confined|strong="H5462"\w* \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w the camp|strong="H4264"\w* \w for seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w*, \w and the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w move on|strong="H5265"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w she|strong="H4813"\w* \w was brought in again|strong="H622"\w*. \v 16 \w After that|strong="H310"\w*, \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Hazeroth|strong="H2698"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w in the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Paran|strong="H6290"\w*.
\c 13
\s1 The Spies Explore Canaan
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 1:19–25|DEU 1:19-25\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w And the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 2 “\w Send out|strong="H7971"\w* for yourself \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w to spy out|strong="H8446"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Canaan|strong="H3667"\w*, \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am giving|strong="H5414"\w* \w to the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w*. \w From each|strong="H3605"\w* \w of their fathers’|strong="H1"\w* \w tribes|strong="H4294"\w* \w send|strong="H7971"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w who is a leader|strong="H5387"\w* among them.”
\p \v 3 \w So at|strong="H5921"\w* \w the command|strong="H6310"\w*\f + \fr 13:3 \ft Literally \fqa according to the mouth\f* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w sent them|strong="H7971"\w* \w out|strong="H853"\w* \w from the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Paran|strong="H6290"\w*. \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w the men|strong="H582"\w* \w were leaders|strong="H7218"\w* \w of the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w*, \v 4 \w and these|strong="H428"\w* \w were their names|strong="H8034"\w*:
\li1 \w From the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Reuben|strong="H7205"\w*, \w Shammua|strong="H8051"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zaccur|strong="H2139"\w*;
\li1 \v 5 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Simeon|strong="H8095"\w*, \w Shaphat|strong="H8202"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Hori|strong="H2753"\w*;
\li1 \v 6 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w Caleb|strong="H3612"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Jephunneh|strong="H3312"\w*;
\li1 \v 7 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Issachar|strong="H3485"\w*, \w Igal|strong="H3008"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Joseph|strong="H3130"\w*;
\li1 \v 8 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Ephraim|strong="H669"\w*, \w Hoshea|strong="H1954"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Nun|strong="H5126"\w*;
\li1 \v 9 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Benjamin|strong="H1144"\w*, \w Palti|strong="H6406"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Raphu|strong="H7505"\w*;
\li1 \v 10 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Zebulun|strong="H2074"\w*, \w Gaddiel|strong="H1427"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Sodi|strong="H5476"\w*;
\li1 \v 11 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H4519"\w* (\w a tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Joseph|strong="H3130"\w*), \w Gaddi|strong="H1426"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Susi|strong="H5485"\w*;
\li1 \v 12 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Dan|strong="H1835"\w*, \w Ammiel|strong="H5988"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Gemalli|strong="H1582"\w*;
\li1 \v 13 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Asher|strong="H836"\w*, \w Sethur|strong="H5639"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Michael|strong="H4317"\w*;
\li1 \v 14 \w from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Naphtali|strong="H5321"\w*, \w Nahbi|strong="H5147"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Vophsi|strong="H2058"\w*;
\li1 \v 15 \w and from the tribe|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Gad|strong="H1410"\w*, \w Geuel|strong="H1345"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Machi|strong="H4352"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w were the names|strong="H8034"\w* \w of the men|strong="H582"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w to spy out|strong="H8446"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w*; \w and Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w gave|strong="H7121"\w* \w to Hoshea|strong="H1954"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Nun|strong="H5126"\w* \w the name Joshua|strong="H3091"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w When Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w to spy out|strong="H8446"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Canaan|strong="H3667"\w*, \w he told|strong="H559"\w* \w them|strong="H413"\w*, “\w Go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w through the Negev|strong="H5045"\w* \w and|strong="H5927"\w* \w into the hill country|strong="H2022"\w*. \v 18 \w See|strong="H7200"\w* \w what|strong="H4100"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w is like|strong="H1931"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w whether its people|strong="H5971"\w* \w are strong|strong="H2389"\w* \w or weak|strong="H7504"\w*, \w few|strong="H4592"\w* \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w many|strong="H7227"\w*. \v 19 \w Is the land|strong="H776"\w* \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w they|strong="H1931"\w* \w live|strong="H3427"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w* \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w bad|strong="H7451"\w*? \w Are the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w they|strong="H1931"\w* \w dwell|strong="H3427"\w* \w open camps|strong="H4264"\w* \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w fortifications|strong="H4013"\w*? \v 20 \w Is the soil|strong="H776"\w* \w fertile|strong="H8082"\w* \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w unproductive|strong="H7330"\w*? \w Are there|strong="H3426"\w* \w trees|strong="H6086"\w* in it \w or|strong="H518"\w* \w not|strong="H369"\w*? \w Be courageous|strong="H2388"\w* \w and bring back|strong="H3947"\w* \w some of the fruit|strong="H6529"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w*.” (\w It was the season|strong="H3117"\w* \w for the first ripe|strong="H1061"\w* \w grapes|strong="H6025"\w*.)
\p \v 21 \w So they went up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and spied out|strong="H8446"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w from the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Zin|strong="H6790"\w* \w as|strong="H5704"\w* \w far as Rehob|strong="H7340"\w*, \w toward Lebo-hamath|strong="H2574"\w*. \v 22 \w They went up|strong="H5927"\w* \w through the Negev|strong="H5045"\w* \w and came|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w Hebron|strong="H2275"\w*, \w where|strong="H8033"\w* \w Ahiman|strong="H289"\w*, \w Sheshai|strong="H8344"\w*, \w and Talmai|strong="H8526"\w*, \w the descendants|strong="H3211"\w* \w of Anak|strong="H6061"\w*, \w dwelled|strong="H2275"\w*. \w It had been built|strong="H1129"\w* \w seven|strong="H7651"\w* \w years|strong="H8141"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w Zoan|strong="H6814"\w* \w in Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*.
\p \v 23 \w When they came|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w the Valley|strong="H5158"\w* \w of Eshcol|strong="H812"\w*,\f + \fr 13:23 \fqa Eshcol \ft means \fqa cluster\ft ; also in verse 24.\f* \w they cut down|strong="H3772"\w* \w a branch|strong="H2156"\w* \w with a single|strong="H259"\w* \w cluster|strong="H811"\w* \w of grapes|strong="H6025"\w*, \w which they carried|strong="H5375"\w* \w on a pole|strong="H4132"\w* \w between two men|strong="H8147"\w*. \w They also took some|strong="H4480"\w* \w pomegranates|strong="H7416"\w* \w and figs|strong="H8384"\w*. \v 24 \w Because of|strong="H5921"\w* \w the cluster|strong="H811"\w* \w of grapes the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w cut|strong="H3772"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*, \w that|strong="H1931"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w was called|strong="H7121"\w* \w the Valley|strong="H5158"\w* \w of Eshcol|strong="H812"\w*.
\s1 The Reports of the Spies
\p \v 25 \w After|strong="H7093"\w* \w forty|strong="H705"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w the men returned|strong="H7725"\w* \w from spying out|strong="H8446"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w*, \v 26 \w and they went back|strong="H1980"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w*, \w and the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Paran|strong="H6290"\w* \w at Kadesh|strong="H6946"\w*. \w They brought back|strong="H7725"\w* \w a report|strong="H1697"\w* \w for the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w and showed|strong="H7200"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w the fruit|strong="H6529"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w*.
\p \v 27 \w And they gave this account|strong="H5608"\w* to Moses: “\w We went|strong="H935"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w to which|strong="H834"\w* \w you sent us|strong="H7971"\w*, \w and indeed|strong="H1571"\w*, \w it|strong="H1931"\w* \w is flowing|strong="H2100"\w* \w with milk|strong="H2461"\w* \w and honey|strong="H1706"\w*. \w Here is|strong="H2088"\w* \w some of its fruit|strong="H6529"\w*! \v 28 \w Nevertheless|strong="H657"\w*, \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w living|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w* \w are strong|strong="H5794"\w*, \w and the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w are large|strong="H1419"\w* \w and fortified|strong="H3966"\w*. \w We even|strong="H1571"\w* \w saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w the descendants|strong="H3211"\w* \w of Anak|strong="H6061"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*. \v 29 \w The Amalekites|strong="H6002"\w* \w live|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of the Negev|strong="H5045"\w*; \w the Hittites|strong="H2850"\w*, \w Jebusites|strong="H2983"\w*, \w and Amorites|strong="H567"\w* \w live|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the hill country|strong="H2022"\w*; \w and the Canaanites|strong="H3669"\w* \w live|strong="H3427"\w* \w by|strong="H5921"\w* \w the sea|strong="H3220"\w* \w and along|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w*.”
\p \v 30 \w Then Caleb|strong="H3612"\w* \w quieted|strong="H2013"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w before|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w We must go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w and take possession of|strong="H3423"\w* \w the land|strong="H853"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w we can certainly conquer|strong="H3201"\w* it!”
\p \v 31 \w But the men|strong="H582"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w had gone up|strong="H5927"\w* \w with him|strong="H5973"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w We cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w go up|strong="H5927"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w they|strong="H1931"\w* \w are stronger|strong="H2389"\w* \w than we are|strong="H4480"\w*!”
\p \v 32 \w So they gave|strong="H3318"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w a bad report|strong="H1681"\w* \w about the land|strong="H776"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w they had spied out|strong="H8446"\w*: “\w The land|strong="H776"\w* \w we explored|strong="H5674"\w* \w devours|strong="H398"\w* \w its inhabitants|strong="H3427"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w we saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w there|strong="H8432"\w* \w are great in stature|strong="H4060"\w*. \v 33 \w We even saw|strong="H7200"\w* \w the Nephilim|strong="H5303"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*— \w the descendants|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Anak|strong="H6061"\w* \w that come from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the Nephilim|strong="H5303"\w*! \w We seemed|strong="H1961"\w* \w like grasshoppers|strong="H2284"\w* \w in our own sight|strong="H5869"\w*, \w and we must have seemed|strong="H1961"\w* \w the same to them|strong="H3651"\w*!”
\c 14
\s1 Israel’s Rebellion
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 1:26–33|DEU 1:26-33\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Then the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w lifted up|strong="H5375"\w* \w their voices|strong="H6963"\w* \w and cried out|strong="H5414"\w*, \w and that|strong="H1931"\w* \w night|strong="H3915"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w wept|strong="H1058"\w*. \v 2 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w grumbled|strong="H3885"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w*, \w and the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*, “\w If only|strong="H3863"\w* \w we had died|strong="H4191"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w if only|strong="H3863"\w* \w we had died|strong="H4191"\w* \w in this|strong="H2088"\w* \w wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*! \v 3 \w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w is the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w bringing|strong="H935"\w* \w us|strong="H853"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w* \w to fall|strong="H5307"\w* \w by the sword|strong="H2719"\w*? \w Our wives|strong="H802"\w* \w and children|strong="H2945"\w* \w will become|strong="H1961"\w* \w plunder|strong="H957"\w*. \w Would it not|strong="H3808"\w* \w be better|strong="H2896"\w* for us \w to go back|strong="H7725"\w* \w to Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*?”
\p \v 4 \w So they said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w one|strong="H376"\w* \w another|strong="H251"\w*, “\w Let us appoint|strong="H5414"\w* \w a leader|strong="H7218"\w* \w and return|strong="H7725"\w* \w to Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*.”
