\c 15
\s1 Laws about Offerings
\p \v 1 \w Then the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \v 2 “\w Speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and tell them|strong="H559"\w*: \w After|strong="H3588"\w* \w you enter|strong="H935"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am giving|strong="H5414"\w* you \w as a home|strong="H4186"\w* \v 3 \w and you present|strong="H6213"\w* \w a food offering|strong="H801"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the herd|strong="H1241"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w flock|strong="H6629"\w* \w to produce|strong="H6213"\w* \w a pleasing|strong="H5207"\w* \w aroma|strong="H7381"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* — \w either a burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w a sacrifice|strong="H2077"\w*, \w for a special|strong="H6381"\w* \w vow|strong="H5088"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w freewill offering|strong="H5071"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w appointed feast|strong="H4150"\w*— \v 4 \w then the one presenting|strong="H7126"\w* \w his offering|strong="H7133"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w shall also present|strong="H7126"\w* \w a grain offering|strong="H4503"\w* \w of a tenth of an ephah|strong="H6241"\w* \w of fine flour|strong="H5560"\w*\f + \fr 15:4 \fqa A tenth of an ephah\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref* dry quarts or 2.2 liters (probably about 2.6 pounds or 1.2 kilograms of flour).\f* \w mixed|strong="H1101"\w* \w with a quarter|strong="H7243"\w* \w hin|strong="H1969"\w* \w of olive oil|strong="H8081"\w*.\f + \fr 15:4 \ft Or \fqa a quarter hin of oil\ft ; that is, \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.97 quarts or 0.92 liters; similarly in verse 5\f* \v 5 \w With|strong="H5921"\w* \w the burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w sacrifice|strong="H2077"\w* \w of each|strong="H259"\w* \w lamb|strong="H3532"\w*, \w you are to prepare|strong="H6213"\w* \w a quarter|str