\p \v 8 \w When|strong="H3588"\w* \w you prepare|strong="H6213"\w* \w a young|strong="H1121"\w* \w bull|strong="H1241"\w* \w as a burnt offering|strong="H5930"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w sacrifice|strong="H2077"\w* \w to fulfill|strong="H6381"\w* \w a vow|strong="H5088"\w* \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w as a peace offering|strong="H8002"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \v 9 \w present|strong="H7126"\w* \w with|strong="H5921"\w* \w the bull|strong="H1241"\w* \w a grain offering|strong="H4503"\w* \w of three-tenths of an ephah|strong="H7969"\w* \w of fine flour|strong="H5560"\w*\f + \fr 15:9 \fqa Three-tenths of an ephah\ft is \ref approximately 6|6\ref* dry quarts or 6.6 liters (probably about 7.6 pounds or 3.5 kilograms of flour).\f* \w mixed|strong="H1101"\w* \w with half|strong="H2677"\w* \w a hin|strong="H1969"\w* \w of olive oil|strong="H8081"\w*.\f + \fr 15:9 \ft Or \fqa half a hin of oil\ft ; that is, \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.9 quarts or 1.8 liters; similarly in verse 10\f* \v 10 \w Also present|strong="H7126"\w* \w half|strong="H2677"\w* \w a hin|strong="H1969"\w* \w of wine|strong="H3196"\w* \w as a drink offering|strong="H5262"\w*. \w It is a food offering|strong="H801"\w*, \w a pleasing|strong="H5207"\w* \w aroma|strong="H7381"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 11 \w This|strong="H3602"\w* \w is to be done|strong="H6213"\w* \w for each|strong="H259"\w* \w bull|strong="H7794"\w*, \w ram|strong="H352"\w*, \w lamb|strong="H7716"\w*, \w or|strong="H176"\w* \w goat|strong="H5795"\w*. \v 12 \w This is how|strong="H3602"\w* \w you must prepare|strong="H6213"\w* \w each one|strong="H259"\w*, \w no matter how|strong="H834"\w* \w many|strong="H4557"\w*.
