\c 16
\s1 Korah’s Rebellion
\p \v 1 \w Now Korah|strong="H7141"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Izhar|strong="H3324"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Kohath|strong="H6955"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Levi|strong="H3881"\w*, \w along with some Reubenites|strong="H7205"\w* — \w Dathan|strong="H1885"\w* \w and Abiram|strong="H48"\w*, \w sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Eliab|strong="H446"\w*, \w and On|strong="H203"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Peleth|strong="H6431"\w* — \w conducted|strong="H3947"\w* \v 2 \w a rebellion|strong="H6965"\w* \w against|strong="H6440"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, \w along with 250|strong="H2572"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w renowned|strong="H8034"\w* \w as leaders|strong="H5387"\w* \w of the congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w and representatives|strong="H7148"\w* \w in the assembly|strong="H4150"\w*. \v 3 \w They came together|strong="H6950"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w and|strong="H5921"\w* \w Aaron|strong="H175"\w* \w and told them|strong="H559"\w*, “\w You have taken too much|strong="H7227"\w* upon yourselves!\f + \fr 16:3 \ft Figuratively \fqa You have gone too far \ft or \fqa You have appropriated too much authority to yourselves\ft ; similarly in verse 7\f* \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w everyone|strong="H3605"\w* \w in the entire|strong="H3605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H5712"\w* \w is holy|strong="H6918"\w*, \w and the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w is in their midst|strong="H8432"\w*. \w Why|strong="H4069"\w* \w then do you exalt|strong="H5375"\w* \w yourselves above|strong="H5921"\w* \w the assembly|strong="H6951"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*?”
