\p \v 21 \w Then Israel|strong="H3478"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w messengers|strong="H4397"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Sihon|strong="H5511"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of the Amorites|strong="H567"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, \v 22 “\w Let us pass|strong="H5674"\w* \w through your land|strong="H776"\w*. \w We will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w turn aside into|strong="H5186"\w* \w any field|strong="H7704"\w* \w or vineyard|strong="H3754"\w*, \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w drink|strong="H8354"\w* \w water|strong="H4325"\w* \w from any well|strong="H875"\w*. \w We will stay on|strong="H1980"\w* \w the King’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w Highway|strong="H1870"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w we have passed through|strong="H5674"\w* \w your territory|strong="H1366"\w*.”
