\p \v 6 \w But Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w asked|strong="H559"\w* \w the Gadites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and Reubenites|strong="H1121"\w*, “\w Shall your brothers|strong="H251"\w* \w go|strong="H935"\w* \w to war|strong="H4421"\w* \w while you|strong="H859"\w* \w sit|strong="H3427"\w* \w here|strong="H6311"\w*? \v 7 \w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w are you discouraging|strong="H5106"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w from crossing|strong="H5674"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has given|strong="H5414"\w* them? \v 8 \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w your fathers|strong="H1"\w* \w did|strong="H6213"\w* \w when I sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w them|strong="H6947"\w* \w from Kadesh-barnea|strong="H6947"\w* \w to inspect|strong="H7200"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w*.
