ne|strong="H6213"\w* \w evil|strong="H7451"\w* \w in His|strong="H3068"\w* \w sight|strong="H5869"\w* \w was gone|strong="H8552"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w Now behold|strong="H2009"\w*, \w you, a brood|strong="H8635"\w* \w of sinners|strong="H2400"\w*, \w have risen up|strong="H6965"\w* \w in place|strong="H8478"\w* \w of your fathers|strong="H1"\w* \w to further|strong="H5750"\w* \w stoke|strong="H5595"\w* \w the burning|strong="H2740"\w* \w anger|strong="H639"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \v 15 \w For if|strong="H3588"\w* \w you turn away|strong="H7725"\w* \w from following Him|strong="H310"\w*, \w He will once again|strong="H3254"\w* \w leave|strong="H5117"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w* \w in the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*, \w and you will be the cause of their destruction|strong="H7843"\w*.”
\p \v 16 \w Then the Gadites and Reubenites approached|strong="H5066"\w* \w Moses|strong="H413"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w We want to build|strong="H1129"\w* \w sheepfolds|strong="H1448"\w* \w here|strong="H6311"\w* \w for our livestock|strong="H4735"\w* \w and cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w for our little ones|strong="H2945"\w*. \v 17 \w But we|strong="H587"\w* \w will arm ourselves|strong="H2502"\w* \w and be ready|strong="H2363"\w*\f + \fr 32:17 \ft LXX \fqa we will arm ourselves for battle\f* \w to go ahead of|strong="H6440"\w* \w the Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w we have brought them|strong="H935"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w their place|strong="H4725"\w*. \w Meanwhile, our little ones|strong="H2945"\w* \w will remain|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the fortified|strong="H4013"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w for protection from|strong="H6440"\w* \w the inhabitants|strong="H3427"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w*. \v 18 \w We will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w return|strong="H7725"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w our homes|strong="H1004"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w every|strong="H376"\w* \w Israelite|strong="H1121"\w* \w has taken possession of|strong="H5157"\w* \w his inheritance|strong="H5159"\w*. \v 19 \w Yet|strong="H3588"\w* \w we will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w have an inheritance|strong="H5157"\w* \w with them|strong="H854"\w* \w across|strong="H5676"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* \w and beyond|strong="H1973"\w*, \w because|strong="H3588"\w* \w our inheritance|strong="H5159"\w* \w has come to us|strong="H413"\w* \w on the east|strong="H4217"\w* \w side|strong="H5676"\w* \w of the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w*.”
\p \v 20 \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w If|strong="H518"\w* \w you will do|strong="H6213"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w*— \w if|strong="H518"\w* \w you will arm yourselves|strong="H2502"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w for battle|strong="H4421"\w*, \v 21 \w and if every one|strong="H3605"\w* \w of your armed men|strong="H2502"\w* \w crosses|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w He has driven|strong="H3423"\w* \w His enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w out before Him|strong="H6440"\w*, \v 22 \w then when the land|strong="H776"\w* \w is subdued|strong="H3533"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w you may return|strong="H7725"\w* \w and be|strong="H1961"\w* \w free|strong="H5355"\w* \w of obligation to the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w and to Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \w And this|strong="H2063"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w* \w will belong|strong="H1961"\w* to you \w as a possession|strong="H272"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 23 \w But if|strong="H518"\w* \w you do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w do|strong="H6213"\w* \w this|strong="H3651"\w*, \w you will certainly|strong="H2009"\w* \w sin|strong="H2398"\w* \w against the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* — \w and be assured that|strong="H3045"\w* \w your sin|strong="H2403"\w* \w will find you out|strong="H4672"\w*. \v 24 \w Build|strong="H1129"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w* for your \w little ones|strong="H2945"\w* \w and folds|strong="H1448"\w* \w for your flocks|strong="H6792"\w*, \w but do|strong="H6213"\w* \w what you have promised|strong="H3318"\w*.”
\p \v 25 \w The Gadites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and Reubenites|strong="H1121"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w*, “\w Your servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w will do|strong="H6213"\w* \w just as|strong="H834"\w* \w our lord|strong="H113"\w* \w commands|strong="H6680"\w*. \v 26 \w Our children|strong="H2945"\w*, \w our wives|strong="H802"\w*, \w our livestock|strong="H4735"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w our animals|strong="H929"\w* \w will remain|strong="H1961"\w* \w here|strong="H8033"\w* \w in the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w of Gilead|strong="H1568"\w*. \v 27 \w But your servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w are equipped|strong="H2502"\w* \w for war|strong="H6635"\w*, \w and every man|strong="H3605"\w* \w will cross over|strong="H5674"\w* \w to the battle|strong="H4421"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w just as|strong="H834"\w* \w our lord|strong="H113"\w* \w says|strong="H1696"\w*.”
\p \v 28 \w So Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w gave orders|strong="H6680"\w* about them \w to Eleazar|strong="H499"\w* \w the priest|strong="H3548"\w*, \w to Joshua|strong="H3091"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Nun|strong="H5126"\w*, \w and to the family|strong="H1"\w* \w leaders|strong="H7218"\w* \w of the tribes|strong="H4294"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*. \v 29 \w And Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*, “\w If|strong="H518"\w* \w the Gadites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and Reubenites|strong="H1121"\w* \w cross|strong="H5674"\w* \w the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w* \w with you|strong="H854"\w*, \w with every|strong="H3605"\w* \w man armed|strong="H2502"\w* \w for battle|strong="H4421"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w and the land|strong="H776"\w* \w is subdued|strong="H3533"\w* \w before you|strong="H6440"\w*, \w then you are to give|strong="H5414"\w* them \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Gilead|strong="H1568"\w* \w as a possession|strong="H272"\w*. \v 30 \w But if|strong="H518"\w* \w they do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w arm themselves|strong="H2502"\w* \w and go across|strong="H5674"\w* \w with you|strong="H854"\w*, \w then they must accept their possession|strong="H270"\w* \w among you|strong="H8432"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Canaan|strong="H3667"\w*.”
\p \v 31 \w The Gadites|strong="H1121"\w* \w and Reubenites|strong="H1121"\w* \w replied|strong="H6030"\w*, “\w As|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has spoken|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w your servants|strong="H5650"\w*, \w so|strong="H3651"\w* \w we will do|strong="H6213"\w*. \v 32 \w We|strong="H5168"\w* \w will cross over|strong="H5674"\w* \w into the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Canaan|strong="H3667"\w* \w armed|strong="H2502"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w that|strong="H854"\w* \w we may have our inheritance|strong="H5159"\w* \w on this side|strong="H5676"\w* \w of the Jordan|strong="H3383"\w*.”
\p \v 33 \w So Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w gave|strong="H5414"\w* to \w the Gadites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w to the Reubenites|strong="H1121"\w*, \w and to the half-tribe|strong="H2677"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H4519"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Joseph|strong="H3130"\w* \w the kingdom|strong="H4467"\w* \w of Sihon|strong="H5511"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of the Amorites|strong="H567"\w* \w and the kingdom|strong="H4467"\w* \w of Og|strong="H5747"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Bashan|strong="H1316"\w* — \w the land|strong="H776"\w* \w including its cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w and the territory|strong="H1367"\w* \w surrounding|strong="H5439"\w* \w them|strong="H5892"\w*.
\p \v 34 \w And the Gadites|strong="H1121"\w* \w built up|strong="H1129"\w* \w Dibon|strong="H1769"\w*, \w Ataroth|strong="H5852"\w*, \w Aroer|strong="H6177"\w*, \v 35 \w Atroth-shophan|strong="H5855"\w*, \w Jazer|strong="H3270"\w*, \w Jogbehah|strong="H3011"\w*, \v 36 \w Beth-nimrah|strong="H1039"\w*, \w and Beth-haran|strong="H1028"\w* \w as fortified|strong="H4013"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w*, \w and they built folds|strong="H1448"\w* \w for their flocks|strong="H6629"\w*.
\p \v 37 \w The Reubenites|strong="H1121"\w* \w built up|strong="H1129"\w* \w Heshbon|strong="H2809"\w*, \w Elealeh|strong="H500"\w*, \w Kiriathaim|strong="H7156"\w*, \v 38 \w as well as Nebo|strong="H5015"\w* \w and Baal-meon|strong="H1186"\w* \w (whose names|strong="H8034"\w* \w were changed|strong="H5437"\w*), \w and Sibmah|strong="H7643"\w*. \w And they renamed|strong="H7121"\w* \w the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w they rebuilt|strong="H1129"\w*.
\p \v 39 \w The descendants|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Machir|strong="H4353"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H4519"\w* \w went|strong="H1980"\w* \w to Gilead|strong="H1568"\w*, \w captured it|strong="H3920"\w*, \w and drove out|strong="H3423"\w* \w the Amorites|strong="H567"\w* \w who were|strong="H834"\w* there. \v 40 \w So Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w gave|strong="H5414"\w* \w Gilead|strong="H1568"\w* \w to the clan of Machir|strong="H4353"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H4519"\w*, \w and they settled|strong="H3427"\w* there. \v 41 \w Jair|strong="H2971"\w*, \w a descendant|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H4519"\w*, \w went|strong="H1980"\w* \w and captured|strong="H3920"\w* \w their villages|strong="H2333"\w* \w and called|strong="H7121"\w* \w them|strong="H2334"\w* \w Havvoth-jair|strong="H2334"\w*.\f + \fr 32:41 \fqa Havvoth-jair \ft means \fqa the villages of Jair\ft .\f* \v 42 \w And Nobah|strong="H5025"\w* \w went|strong="H1980"\w* \w and captured|strong="H3920"\w* \w Kenath|strong="H7079"\w* \w and its villages|strong="H1323"\w* \w and called|strong="H7121"\w* it \w Nobah|strong="H5025"\w*, \w after his own name|strong="H8034"\w*.
\c 33
\s1 Forty-Two Journeys of the Israelites
\p \v 1 \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w are the journeys|strong="H4550"\w* \w of the Israelites|strong="H3478"\w* \w when|strong="H834"\w* \w they came out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w* \w by their divisions|strong="H6635"\w* \w under the leadership|strong="H3027"\w* \w of Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w and Aaron|strong="H175"\w*. \v 2 \w At|strong="H5921"\w* \w the LORD’s|strong="H3068"\w* \w command|strong="H6310"\w*, \w Moses|strong="H4872"\w* \w recorded|strong="H3789"\w* \w the stages|strong="H4161"\w* \w of their journey|strong="H4550"\w*. \w These|strong="H428"\w* \w are the stages|strong="H4550"\w* \w listed by their starting points|strong="H4161"\w*:
\li1 \v 3 \w On the fifteenth|strong="H2568"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w* \w of the first|strong="H7223"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w*, \w on|strong="H7223"\w* \w the day after|strong="H4283"\w* \w the Passover|strong="H6453"\w*, \w the Israelites set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Rameses|strong="H7486"\w*. \w They|strong="H1121"\w* \w marched out|strong="H3318"\w* \w defiantly|strong="H3027"\w*\f + \fr 33:3 \ft Or \fqa marched out boldly\ft ; literally \fqa marched out with an upraised hand\f* \w in full view|strong="H5869"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the Egyptians|strong="H4713"\w*, \v 4 \w who|strong="H4713"\w* \w were burying|strong="H6912"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w their firstborn|strong="H1060"\w*, \w whom the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had struck down|strong="H5221"\w* among them; \w for the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w had executed|strong="H6213"\w* \w judgment|strong="H8201"\w* \w against their gods|strong="H430"\w*. \v 5 \w The Israelites|strong="H1121"\w* \w set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Rameses|strong="H7486"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Succoth|strong="H5523"\w*.
\li1 \v 6 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Succoth|strong="H5523"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Etham|strong="H864"\w*, \w on the edge|strong="H7097"\w* \w of the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*.
\li1 \v 7 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Etham|strong="H864"\w* \w and turned back|strong="H7725"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w Pi-hahiroth|strong="H6367"\w*, \w opposite|strong="H5921"\w* \w Baal-zephon|strong="H1189"\w*, \w and they camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w near|strong="H6440"\w* \w Migdol|strong="H4024"\w*.
\li1 \v 8 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from|strong="H6440"\w* \w Pi-hahiroth|strong="H6367"\w*\f + \fr 33:8 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, SP, and Vulgate; see verse 7; most MT manuscripts \fqa Hahiroth\f* \w and crossed|strong="H5674"\w* \w through|strong="H8432"\w* \w the sea|strong="H3220"\w*, \w into the wilderness|strong="H4057"\w*, \w and they journeyed three days|strong="H7969"\w* \w into the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Etham|strong="H864"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Marah|strong="H4785"\w*.
\li1 \v 9 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Marah|strong="H4785"\w* \w and came|strong="H935"\w* \w to Elim|strong="H362"\w*, \w where there were twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w springs|strong="H5869"\w* \w and seventy|strong="H7657"\w* \w palm trees|strong="H8558"\w*, \w and they camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*.
\li1 \v 10 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Elim|strong="H362"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w by|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Red|strong="H5488"\w* \w Sea|strong="H3220"\w*.\f + \fr 33:10 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\ft ; also in verse 11\f*
\li1 \v 11 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from the Red|strong="H5488"\w* \w Sea|strong="H3220"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w in the Desert|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Sin|strong="H5512"\w*.\f + \fr 33:11 \ft The geographical name \fqa Sin \ft is related to \fqa Sinai \ft and should not be mistaken for the English word \fqa sin\ft ; also in verse 12.\f*
\li1 \v 12 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from the Desert|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Sin|strong="H5512"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Dophkah|strong="H1850"\w*.
\li1 \v 13 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Dophkah|strong="H1850"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Alush|strong="H442"\w*.
\li1 \v 14 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Alush|strong="H442"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Rephidim|strong="H7508"\w*, \w where|strong="H8033"\w* \w there was|strong="H1961"\w* \w no|strong="H3808"\w* \w water|strong="H4325"\w* \w for the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w to drink|strong="H8354"\w*.
\li1 \v 15 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Rephidim|strong="H7508"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w in the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Sinai|strong="H5514"\w*.
\li1 \v 16 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from the Wilderness|strong="H4057"\w* \w of Sinai|strong="H5514"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Kibroth-hattaavah|strong="H6914"\w*.
\li1 \v 17 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from|strong="H6914"\w* \w Kibroth-hattaavah|strong="H6914"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Hazeroth|strong="H2698"\w*.
\li1 \v 18 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Hazeroth|strong="H2698"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Rithmah|strong="H7575"\w*.
\li1 \v 19 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Rithmah|strong="H7575"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Rimmon-perez|strong="H7428"\w*.
\li1 \v 20 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from|strong="H7428"\w* \w Rimmon-perez|strong="H7428"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Libnah|strong="H3841"\w*.
\li1 \v 21 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Libnah|strong="H3841"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Rissah|strong="H7446"\w*.
\li1 \v 22 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Rissah|strong="H7446"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Kehelathah|strong="H6954"\w*.
\li1 \v 23 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Kehelathah|strong="H6954"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Mount|strong="H2022"\w* \w Shepher|strong="H8234"\w*.
\li1 \v 24 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Mount|strong="H2022"\w* \w Shepher|strong="H8234"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Haradah|strong="H2732"\w*.
\li1 \v 25 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Haradah|strong="H2732"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Makheloth|strong="H4722"\w*.
\li1 \v 26 \w They set out|strong="H5265"\w* \w from Makheloth|strong="H4722"\w* \w and camped|strong="H2583"\w* \w at Tahath|strong="H8480"\w*.
